From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:01:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Read the patched firmware feed file instead of the
 releases API

The patched firmware check listed consnop/PebbleOS's releases through
api.github.com, whose unauthenticated quota is 60 requests an hour per IP.
Behind a carrier NAT or public Wi-Fi that quota is shared with everyone
else, so the check kept failing as rate limited.

The firmware pipeline now attaches firmware-feed.json to each release
(tag, publish time, and per board the asset name, size and sha256). Gravel
fetches it from releases/latest/download/, which the API quota doesn't
cover, and decodes it itself since release downloads are served as
application/octet-stream. The download URL is built from the tag and the
expected asset name rather than taken from the feed, and the tag must look
like <upstream tag>-consnop-<8 hex> because it becomes part of that URL.

